      "content": "This phenomenon is often referred to as \"vibrational fatigue\" or \"resonant behavior,\" where the pallets resonate with the floor's natural vibrations. This can be due to the pallets' weight, shape, and material, as well as the Dynamics Permanent Normal Strain (DPNS) or the Positive Die Stress (PDS) in the racking system. You may also consider using anti-vibration mounting systems or visiting a pallet received with a resultant force less than 10Defs (DPNS or PDS), however the issue could be caused by floating pallets or Media-Flo separation on the pallets relegated onboard.",
